**VM state shape and closure representation.** `DebruijnVM` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_vm.cljc`) carries exactly the design's 8 fields (`:segment :pc :frames :free-env :stack :continuation :store :status`) plus two composition-level fields not part of the transition state: `:primitives` and `:modules`, needed to give `:load-free` the same `env -> store -> primitives -> module registry` order `engine/resolve-var` already implements — mirrored on `SemanticVM`, which likewise carries fields beyond its four CESK-state accessors. A closure value is `{:type :closure, :arity n, :body-pc pc, :frames captured-frames}`; it carries no `:macro?` field, confirmed by inspection of section 2's instruction shape — this is a positional dimension and never had one.

**Frame direction.** Frame 0 for `:load-bound` is the innermost frame, read from the end of `:frames`. Concrete example from `nested-closure-capture-test`: after the outer closure `(fn [x] ...)` is called with `3` and the inner closure `(fn [y] ...)` is called with `4`, `:frames` is `[[3] [4]]`. Inside the inner body, `[:load-bound 1 0]` reaches `x` (depth 1 → index `2-1-1=0` → frame `[3]`) and `[:load-bound 0 0]` reaches `y` (depth 0 → index `1` → frame `[4]`).

**Reuse vs. fresh.** Reused directly: `yin.vm.engine/resolve-var` for `:load-free` (signature `[env store primitives registry name]` fit `:free-env`/`:store`/`:primitives`/`:modules` without adaptation, so no equivalent was written). Written fresh: `bind-positional` (the positional `bind-params` equivalent, `(vec (take arity (concat args (repeat nil))))`), and `frame-value` (innermost-at-end addressing) — both new, positional-only concepts with no named-VM analogue to call. `:call`'s primitive-function branch (`(apply f args)`) is a minimal fresh reimplementation of the pure half of `apply-call`'s `fn?` case (`yin.vm.semantic.cljc`), without its effect-handling branch, since FFI/effects are B4's.

